# v8.44: amendments to the complete v8.43 source (parent SHA256
# 2442a881dc211b516ba5f2da1ef4443393c5c54b2f4cb2f5f44f8f15d96257a9 as supplied).
# (1) Control-arm Q candidates (SL.*.control_arm): base learner fitted on the
#     unexposed training rows only, A removed from its design; exposed-arm
#     prediction = control-arm prediction + one weighted shift. Implemented and
#     tested, but OFF in the primary Q library, which is unchanged from v8.43.
#     Sensitivity D13_Q_control_arm adds them (and learners$ranger$always_split_A).
# (2) g_calibration_method = "select": identity vs Platt chosen inside each outer
#     training fold by survey-weighted log-loss cross-validated over the inner
#     whole-PSU folds. Isotonic stays available as an explicit method and in the
#     offline comparison, but is NOT an automatic candidate: its top block is
#     degenerate at 1, which sends high-score comparison units to the upper
#     propensity bound and inflates the ATT odds weights.
# (3) exposure$exposure_mode: "wave3_complete" (bridge) and "durable_control"
#     (secondary contrast). Default "wave2_only" leaves the primary unchanged.
# (4) Preflight repair: the v8.42 two-part-MNAR immutability check compared
#     serialize() bytes, which differ once R expands a deferred as.character()
#     vector even though the object is unchanged; it now compares values.
# The amended source passed its native preflight and an end-to-end run on
# entirely synthetic files (R 4.3.3; SuperLearner 2.0-29, glmnet 4.1-8,
# ranger 0.16.0, xgboost 1.7.8.1, survey 4.4-2). It has NOT been run on Add
# Health data. Run the enabled native preflight in the production environment.
#
# v8.43: reviewer amendments to the complete v8.42 source.
# (1) A is unpenalized in elastic-net Q, pi and A-conditioned auxiliary fits;
#     ordinary W coefficients remain regularized. Actual g(A|W) is unchanged
#     as an algorithm; excluding birth-record predictors can change its fit.
# (2) birth_records and registered/recognizable derivatives are excluded from W.
#     The source is retained for provenance; sample/outcome construction is unchanged.
# (3) Optional multi-seed ATT output uses repeated-split median aggregation with
#     median[within-split SE^2 + squared deviation from the median ATT].
#     Splits are NOT independent datasets; there is no division by seed count.
#     The optional multi-seed stage remains OFF. The ordinary primary is one fit.
# The v8.42 residual-Q architecture and existing ATT/MNAR diagnostics are retained.
# (v8.43 itself was not executed in native R in its authoring environment.)
# Run the enabled native preflight before production; do not bypass a failure.
# Parent SHA256: 8f3712d63826491b3dac5b2888d499ce828723367289e828a1d18665dc1a2517
#
# Historical v8.42 notes below describe changes from v8.41; v8.43 amendments above supersede them.
# v8.42: bounded outer-training ensemble-residual Q update.
# Based on the uploaded v8.41 source; existing estimand, sample, outcome rules,
# g/pi/status models, caps, rare-category safeguards and survey inference remain.
# The residual candidate reuses the fitted core/broad Q library's training-side
# prediction information. Residual screening and one joint recipe are learned
# once per outer training fold. The final elastic net uses the SAME inner PSU
# partitions as the old Q candidates. Outer-validation outcomes remain unused.
# IMPORTANT: this is NOT fully nested screener-learner validation. Legacy
# screens and mixture weights also use outer-training outcomes. The ensemble
# residual is a TRAINING HEURISTIC, not independent evidence of model accuracy.
# No separate pilot glmnet and no added nonlinear candidate are fitted.
# Existing q_validate/q_resid_val outputs gain an aggregate att_control row.
# mnar_two_part adds an explicitly labelled observed-unresolved-pattern
# sensitivity, not a new primary missingness estimator or scenario confidence CI.
# All respondent-linked checkpoints remain inside the restricted workspace.
# Keep preflight enabled. Native R execution was not available in the authoring
# environment; static checks do not replace the mandatory R integration tests.
# Native production runtime has not been benchmarked.
