    # v8.37 g-ONLY clipping sweep. The legacy sweep above moves the g and pi
    # bounds together, which confounds the two. These rows move the g floor
    # alone and hold pi at its configured bounds, so the reported difference is
    # attributable to g truncation. For the ATT the control contribution enters
    # through g/(1-g), which is bounded ABOVE by g_upper and is numerically
    # stable as g -> 0, so a large lower bound buys little stability for this
    # estimand while inducing truncation bias.
    att_g_only_clip_floors = c(0.005, 0.01, 0.025, 0.05),
    # Sample-size-based lower bound c/(sqrt(n) * log(n)) of Gruber, Phillips,
    # Lee & van der Laan (Am J Epidemiol 2022;191:1640-1651), the default in
